---

The LoCoMo benchmark judge in
benchmarks/Mneme.Benchmarks.LoCoMo/Clients.cs (MemAlignedJudge) re-expresses
the LoCoMo J-score grading methodology (partial credit, paraphrase tolerance,
date/duration tolerance, semantic-overlap / same-referent leniency) used by
Mem0's public benchmark suite (https://github.com/mem0ai/memory-benchmarks,
Apache 2.0) so Mneme's LoCoMo numbers are comparable to Mem0's published
figures. No upstream prompt text is copied verbatim; the rules are
re-implemented in Mneme's own wording. The harness also mirrors Mem0's scoring
scope by reporting a "Mem0-comparable" subtotal over LoCoMo categories 1–4
(adversarial / category 5 excluded, matching their CATEGORIES_TO_EVALUATE).
